  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: JacksonXml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: JacksonXml\n       Program: jackson-dataformat-xml\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JacksonXml/JacksonXml.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/jackson-dataformat-xml.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JacksonXml/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 6\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: JacksonXml-5\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n8aa276ba6b2092a562195f9a94eb562686a3352c\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2018-05-21 12:28:21 -0700\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\n282\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-dataformat-xml/issues/282\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - com.fasterxml.jackson.dataformat.xml.MapperCopyTest::testCopyWith\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Should NOT use name 'AnnotatedName' but 'Pojo282', xml = <AnnotatedName><a>3</a></AnnotatedName>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - com.fasterxml.jackson.dataformat.xml.ser.XmlSerializerProvider\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: `@JacksonXmlRootElement` malfunction when using it with multiple `XmlMapper`s and disabling annotations\nState: closed\n\nDescription:\nFound this in version 2.9.4 running some tests that go back and forth serializing with an XML mapper that uses annotations, and another one that ignores them. May be related to issue #171 and the cache of class annotations.\r\n\r\nWhen running this code, the second print statement should use the annotation's localName but it instead uses the class name.\r\n\r\n```\r\n@JacksonXmlRootElement(localName = \"myname\")\r\npublic class XMLTest {\r\n\r\n    public static void main(String[] s) throws Exception {\r\n\r\n        final ObjectMapper xmlMapper = new XmlMapper();\r\n        final ObjectMapper noAnnotationsXmlMapper = xmlMapper.copy()\r\n                .configure(MapperFeature.USE_ANNOTATIONS, false)\r\n                .configure(SerializationFeature.FAIL_ON_EMPTY_BEANS, false);\r\n\r\n        System.out.println(noAnnotationsXmlMapper.writeValueAsString(new XMLTest()));\r\n        System.out.println(xmlMapper.writeValueAsString(new XMLTest()));\r\n\r\n    }\r\n\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<XMLTest/>\r\n<XMLTest/>\r\n```\n\nComments:\n\n[cowtowncoder]: Ok, does sound like caching of root names might be causing the issue here.\n\n[cowtowncoder]: Turned out to be inadvertent sharing of root name lookup cache. Was resolved for 3.0 (due to the way construction changed), but test now covers 2.9 and 3.0. Fix will be in `2.9.6`.",
  "fix_diff": ""
